WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.918
My name is Daniel Felt,

00:00:11.918 --> 00:00:13.676
and I am the owner of Kura Home.

00:00:13.676 --> 00:00:15.410
Today, we are going to
go through the process

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.080
of deep cleaning air ducts.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.950
The purpose of an air duct is essentially

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.978
to provide fresh, clean air to your home.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.490
We provide air-duct cleaning

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.200
and routine home-maintenance services

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.882
where we visit our clients'
homes once a quarter

00:00:27.882 --> 00:00:29.158
and do everything you're
supposed to be doing

00:00:29.158 --> 00:00:30.200
as a perfect homeowner

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.700
but a lot of people don't have the time

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.560
or neglect to do.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.567
When we clean the air ducts,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.690
we go through and we
clean the entire system.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.098
So we start in the upper level,

00:00:38.098 --> 00:00:41.060
and we work our way all the
way through the entire home.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.610
Depending on who and what
is living in the home,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.669
the debris that we find
inside of air ducts

00:00:45.669 --> 00:00:47.250
consists of a lot of different items,

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.667
such as skin cells, dust,

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.150
dander, pet debris, pet hair.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.790
Anything that you would see when you

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.210
maybe wipe your feet off on a rug

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.400
when you walk inside a home

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.150
can be found inside of an air duct.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.020
This air duct has not been cleaned

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.510
for probably 50-plus years.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.890
Additionally, the person
that lived in this home

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.550
has also smoked and had pets.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.790
So this is a very severe air duct

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:12.930
that you can actually smell it.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:17.100
It has a old-house smell
built up over time.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.600
If it's a really light color,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.400
often we're finding
sawdust or Sheetrock dust

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.320
that is from construction debris.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.580
As we get into darker colors,

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.210
sometimes smoking inside the home

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.500
is going to leave more of a yellow color.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.540
And as it gets darker, a lot of times

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.500
we're more concerned
about a humidity issue

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.800
that can eventually turn
into a dark-colored mold.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.790
You're getting into more
hazardous material in there.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.600
Once the air-duct cover is removed,

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.870
we are going to allow
the air-compressor hose

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.940
to be put into the air duct.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.640
Before we're turning on that hose,

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.900
we're going to put a
clear dome over the cover

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.570
and we're going to attach
our HEPA vacuum to the dome.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.040
Once those items are in place,

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.290
we're going to turn the air compressor on,

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:56.010
and that allows the hose
with a reverse-blasting ball

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.930
to propel itself forward
into the air duct.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.900
The clear dome that's used is crucial

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.740
because it creates a sealed environment

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:03.765
so that we're getting all the dust

00:02:03.765 --> 00:02:04.848
and debris out of the home and we're not

00:02:04.848 --> 00:02:07.030
creating a mess inside the home.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:08.460
But it's also crucial because it creates

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.660
a really nice suction area.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.080
So all of the power
from the air compressor

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.060
and the vacuum are working together

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.800
to pull and push the debris outside.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.080
We can twist and turn that hose,

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.960
so we can go around any corner.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.680
Once we get to the end trunk line,

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.990
we can feel that in the
air-compressor hose,

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.120
and we're going to slowly pull that back

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.260
at about 1 foot per second.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.482
As we're doing that,
we can see all the dust

00:02:31.482 --> 00:02:33.590
and debris that is being
removed from the air duct

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.906
come through that clear dome

00:02:34.906 --> 00:02:37.314
and go into the HEPA vacuum.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.600
Once we've completed the cleaning,

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.240
we find that a little
bit of dust and debris

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.420
has come all the way at
the end of the air duct.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.220
And it's really important
to take your vacuum

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.408
and clean out that extra
debris that's come.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.460
Oftentimes, that's where
you're going to find

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.590
the real treasures, such as bugs, toys,

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.370
dog toys, bones, items like that

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.620
that have been placed
really far into the air duct

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.763
and all of our equipment
has pulled it out.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.240
In order to clean the dust and debris

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.570
that's found on the inside
or outside of vents,

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.300
you want to remove the vent first

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.240
and brush that off with the vacuum,

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.174
and you're going to get a majority

00:03:13.174 --> 00:03:14.540
of dust and debris off.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.900
Then we put the vent cover back on

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.610
and replace the screws
back to the original format

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.310
and make sure the area is nice and clean

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.625
and clear of debris.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.050
All the air in your home is circulating

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.580
through your furnace on a regular basis.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.730
And by having a clean,
clear furnace filter,

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.630
it's going to catch
all the dust and debris

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.890
that is circulating throughout.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.290
Depending on the style of
furnace filter that you have,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.677
you may have one that needs to be cleaned

00:03:38.677 --> 00:03:40.533
on a regular basis, and you can do this

00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:42.900
by using a HEPA vacuum and brush.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.570
Locate the furnace filter
inside your furnace

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.220
and remove that door and
pull that furnace filter out.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.860
The next thing you want
to do is take your vacuum

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.830
and place that over the furnace filter

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:52.946
to make sure you're cleaning that

00:03:52.946 --> 00:03:54.905
really nice and thoroughly.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.340
A dryer vent is allowing
the exhaust from a dryer

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.580
to be pushed outside of the home.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.460
The reason why is because, over time,

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.153
lint builds up inside that dryer vent.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.130
To properly clean a dryer vent,

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.380
usually you just need an air compressor,

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.960
and you can use a
reverse-blasting ball or whip

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.143
to place inside the dryer vent.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.680
We're going to find that exhaust

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.820
on the outside of the home,

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.170
and we're going to place
the air-compressor hose

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.150
inside the dryer vent,

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.420
and we're going to turn that on.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.460
That will propel itself into the dryer

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.730
and dislodge all of the lint
that's built up over time.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.196
There's heat that's being pushed

00:04:37.196 --> 00:04:38.354
through that dryer vent,

00:04:38.354 --> 00:04:41.870
and if the dryer vent does
not have proper airflow,

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.058
it's very easy for that lint

00:04:44.058 --> 00:04:46.390
to become flammable and start on fire.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.800
We recommend having
your dryer vent cleaned

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.550
on an annual basis to prevent
the buildup of the lint

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.603
and decrease the chance of a
fire happening in your home.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.620
Depending on your current health,

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:00.040
such as if you have really
bad allergies or not,

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.790
that can play a really large factor

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.615
on the risk of living in a home

00:05:03.615 --> 00:05:05.206
with the dirty air ducts.

00:05:05.206 --> 00:05:06.810
We've had all kinds of different results.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.170
We've had people that have told us

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.750
that they slept through the
night for the first time

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.900
after they had their air ducts cleaned,

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.742
because the air quality
was improved that much.

